     "title": "Apple trained its own AI model for China with help from Alibaba",
     "url": "https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/980160/apple-intelligence-china-custom-ai-model-alibaba",
     "time": "08-14 17:30",
     "ts": 1786699810,
     "summary": "Apple has reportedly trained a custom AI model for the China market alongside domestic tech giant Alibaba, a rare cross-border partnership that cuts across grow",
     "source": "The Verge AI",
     "content": "Apple has reportedly trained a custom AI model for the China market alongside domestic tech giant Alibaba, a rare cross-border partnership that cuts across growing tensions between Beijing and Washington.\nApple trained its own AI model for China with help from Alibaba\nThe rare US-China partnership comes as Apple prepares to roll out its on-device generative AI service in China.\nThe rare US-China partnership comes as Apple prepares to roll out its on-device generative AI service in China.\nThe China-focused large language model was developed in partnership with Alibaba and trained with the company’s support, Reuters reports, citing three unnamed people familiar with the matter.\nDeveloping a custom model of its own marks a departure from Apple’s previous strategy in the country and would give the company more control over its products in the competitive Chinese smartphone market. Historically, Apple has used domestic Chinese models to bring generative AI to its devices sold there, as the US models it uses elsewhere — like OpenAI’s ChatGPT — aren’t available.\nThe report comes as Apple gears up to release Apple Intelligence in China. Sources told Reuters this should happen “in the coming months after an update to its iOS operating system.” Apple officially registered the on-device generative AI service with China’s cyberspace regulator last month, clearing a major regulatory hurdle for device rollout.\nThe China-focused model gives Apple a leg up as a US company navigating Beijing’s difficult regulatory landscape, particularly given escalating tensions surrounding AI development in recent months. AI models must be registered with and cleared by the government in China before public release. It would also make Apple the first US company approved to offer a proprietary AI model in China, according to Reuters.\nApple did not immediately respond to The Verge’s request for comment.\nMost Popular\n- Marvel reveals the new X-Men cast, including Inde Navarrette and Adam Driver\n- We’re reaching peak camera with the Sony A7R VI\n- I finally found a magnetic phone grip I never want to remove\n- Xteink’s tiny e-readers are getting access to free books through Libby\n- Disney D23 2026: Everything announced for Star Wars, Marvel, and more",
     "_extract_method": "trafilatura",
     "zh": "苹果联合阿里巴巴为中国训练专属AI模型",
     "content_zh": "据路透社报道，苹果为适配中国市场，联合国内科技巨头阿里巴巴共同开发了面向中国的大语言模型，这是中美关系紧张背景下罕见的跨过合作。此前苹果在中国市场部署生成式AI多使用本土模型，此次自研专属模型是为即将在中国推出的Apple Intelligence服务做准备，也便于苹果在竞争激烈的中国智能手机市场掌握更多产品控制权。"
