     "title": "Making the data center business case",
     "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/15/making-the-data-center-business-case/",
     "time": "08-15 12:00",
     "ts": 1786766400,
     "summary": "A data center can be built in 18 to 24 months, but connecting it to the grid is another matter, writes Laura Hoffmann-Ostenhof, Europe industry lead at modeling",
     "source": "pv magazine",
     "content": "Making the data center business case\n    \t\tA data center can be built in 18 to 24 months, but connecting it to the grid is another matter, writes Laura Hoffmann-Ostenhof, Europe industry lead at modeling software supplier Gridcog. Across Europe’s established hubs – the FLAP-D cluster of Frankfurt, London, Amsterdam, Paris and Dublin – the wait for a grid connection now runs from seven to 10 years, as data centers compete for capacity.    \nThe scale is easy to underestimate. The pipeline for data centers in the Europe, Middle East and Africa (EMEA) region is growing more than 40% year on year. FLAP-D available data center capacity has fallen to around 6%, with over 80% of it pre-let before completion. Yet most building is happening outside Europe. BloombergNEF counted …\n            Advertisement        \n        \n                Advertisement        \n        \n                Advertisement        \n        \n                Advertisement",
     "_extract_method": "trafilatura",
     "zh": "数据中心业务可行性分析",
     "content_zh": "建模软件供应商Gridcog欧洲行业负责人Laura Hoffmann-Ostenof指出，数据中心建设需18至24个月，但并网难度更大。欧洲法兰克福、伦敦、阿姆斯特丹、巴黎、都柏林组成的FLAP-D成熟数据中心枢纽，当前并网等待周期达7至10年，各数据中心争抢容量资源。欧洲、中东和非洲（EMEA）地区数据中心项目管线年增速超40%，FLAP-D可用数据中心容量已降至约6%，超80%的容量在竣工前已被预租，且当前大部分新建项目集中在欧洲以外地区。"
