     "title": "Limes reaches RTB stage for 200MW/1GWh Huañil BESS project in Chile",
     "url": "https://www.energy-storage.news/limes-reaches-rtb-stage-200mw-1gwh-huanil-bess-project-chile/",
     "time": "08-15 00:02",
     "ts": 1786723371,
     "summary": "Italian clean energy developer Limes Renewable Energy has reached the ready-to-build stage at its 200MW/1GWh Huañil project.",
     "source": "Energy Storage News",
     "content": "Italian clean energy developer Limes Renewable Energy has reached the ready-to-build stage at its 200MW/1GWh Huañil project.\nThe project is located in the Coquimbo region, just north of the capital Santiago, and is the company’s largest battery energy storage system (BESS) in Chile. The project and joins a portfolio that includes two other BESS, currently in development with a combined power of 350MW, and the Pradera Larga solar-plus-storage project, which aims to pair 84MW of solar PV capacity with 90MW of BESS.\nThe Huañil project is also the company’s first to reach the RTB stage outside of Italy, and Limes said that the Pradera Larga project, and one standalone BESS in Chile, would advance towards the RTB stage “in the coming months”.\n“Bringing our first Chilean project to RTB is a defining moment for us in the region, and one that reflects years of disciplined groundwork,” said Limes head of LATAM Martin Libra. “With our pipeline maturing and two more projects moving towards RTB, we’re well positioned to advance the strategic partnerships that will define our next phase of growth in Chile.”\nTry Premium for just $1\n- Full premium access for the first month at only $1\n- Converts to an annual rate after 30 days unless cancelled\n- Cancel anytime during the trial period\nPremium Benefits\n- Expert industry analysis and interviews\n- Digital access to PV Tech Power journal\n- Exclusive event discounts\nOr get the full Premium subscription right away\nOr continue reading this article for free\nChile has seen a number of significant project developments already this year, led by the inauguration of a 3.5GWh component of Grenergy’s Oasis de Atacama solar-plus-storage project. Commissioned in phases, the project was initially planned to have 11GWh of BESS, and this goal has since been expanded to 14GWh.\nOther project news includes ContourGlobal starting construction at a 90MW/360MWh BESS project, to be paired with a 131MW solar PV project, and Verano Energy selecting Sungrow to supply BESS to its 152MW/606MWh Observatorio project in O’Higgins, central Chile.\nThe news follows a number of project advancements for Limes, such as the securing of environmental approvals for three projects, including Huañil, since last November. The company is also active in the renewable energy generation sector, and last summer sold a 287MW portfolio of solar PV and wind asses to an unnamed independent power producer (IPP).",
     "_extract_method": "trafilatura",
     "zh": "Limes公司智利200MW/1GWh华尼尔储能项目进入可建设阶段",
     "content_zh": "意大利清洁能源开发商Limes Renewable Energy旗下位于智利科金博大区的200MW/1GWh华尼尔电池储能项目已进入可建设阶段，这是该公司在智利最大的储能项目，也是其首个在意大利之外进入可建设阶段的项目。目前Limes在智利还有总装机350MW的两个储能项目、84MW光伏配90MW储能的普拉德拉拉尔加光储项目正在开发，后两个项目也将于数月内进入可建设阶段。该公司拉美负责人表示，华尼尔项目落地是其在拉美区域发展的里程碑，随着项目管线成熟，公司将推进战略合作，加速在智利的下一步布局。"
