     "title": "Anthropic revenue reportedly jumps to more than $11.5 billion in second quarter",
     "url": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/15/anthropic-revenue-jumps-to-over-11point5-billion-in-q2-report.html",
     "time": "08-15 22:45",
     "ts": 1786805131,
     "summary": "The jump in revenue underscores the rapid growth of the Claude chatbot maker as it prepares for a potential blockbuster initial public offering.",
     "source": "CNBC",
     "content": "Anthropic's revenue surged more than 14-fold in the second quarter from a year earlier, Bloomberg News reported Friday, underscoring the rapid growth of the Claude chatbot maker as it prepares for a potential blockbuster initial public offering.\nThe AI company reported preliminary revenue of more than $11.5 billion for its latest completed quarter, up from $787 million in the same period last year and $4.73 billion in the first quarter of 2026, according to documents viewed by Bloomberg News.\nAnthropic also posted positive adjusted operating income in the second quarter, according to the documents. The figures are preliminary and could still change, Bloomberg reported.\nAn Anthropic spokesperson did not immediately respond to a CNBC request for comment.\nThe jump in revenue comes as Anthropic competes with OpenAI for corporate customers and has gained traction among professionals using its software for tasks including coding.\nAnthropic said in May that its run-rate revenue crossed $47 billion, up from roughly $10 billion in revenue in all of 2025.\nAnthropic's early meetings with prospective investors ahead of its potential IPO have been high-level and have not included discussions about specific financials or a valuation, sources told CNBC's David Faber on Thursday. Anthropic CFO Krishna Rao is leading the meetings, the sources said.\nAn IPO as soon as this fall could make Anthropic one of the first major private AI companies to tap public markets. That debut would unlock access to billions of dollars in additional capital, providing the immense financial runway required to fund escalating compute infrastructure costs, secure advanced hardware, and build specialized data centers.",
     "_extract_method": "trafilatura",
     "zh": "报道称Anthropic第二季度营收跃升至逾115亿美元",
     "content_zh": "彭博社报道称，Anthropic第二季度营收同比激增超14倍，初步数据达逾115亿美元，远高于去年同期的7.87亿美元和2026年第一季度的47.3亿美元；其二季度经调整营业利润也实现转正，不过相关数据为初步统计，仍可能调整。目前Anthropic正与OpenAI争夺企业客户，其软件在编程等专业场景中颇受欢迎；今年5月该公司曾表示年化营收已突破470亿美元，2025年全年营收约100亿美元，眼下正为潜在IPO接触意向投资者。"
